Package: homesynapse
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: NexSys HomeSynapse <homesynapse@nexsys.example>
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: adduser
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://nexsys.example/homesynapse
Description: HomeSynapse Core — local-first smart-home engine
 A local-first, event-sourced smart-home operating system that runs entirely on
 your own hardware. Installs as a least-privilege systemd service, loopback-bound
 and authenticated by default.
 .
 This package is self-contained: it bundles its own jlinked Java runtime, so no
 system JDK is required and nothing is fetched from the network at install time.
 On first start it mints a one-time pairing token; run `homesynapse-token` to see
 where it landed, then pair a client to reach the dashboard.
